  "body": "Antigravity CLI (agy) conversations are now listed on the Sessions page (internal/sessions/agy.go), but only from the Windows/macOS/Linux home's `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli`. An agy inside a WSL distro is not read: `allFiles` has no `wslFiles(\"agy\")`, and `agyCallFiles` (#2097) doesn't read WSL either, so neither its sessions nor its calls show on Windows when agy runs in WSL.\n\nTo do: add agy to the WSL session and call readers (`wslFiles` needs a lister for agy's `brain/<id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl` and its `conversation_summaries.db`, read through `\\\\wsl.localhost`), and a resume through `wslResume`. `resumeCommand` leaves `AgyStart` (magpie's launch command) out for a WSL distro on purpose: the Windows twin's key and address are not the distro's.\n\nLeft alone in the commit that lists agy's sessions; not tried on a real WSL agy.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
