   "body": "The WSL readers are in, on [fix/agy-wsl-sessions](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/agy-wsl-sessions) (`96311a8a`, based on today's `main`):\n\n- `wslFiles` lists agy now — `wslAgents` gained `.gemini/antigravity-cli`, and `wslScan` reads its `brain/<id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl` and `conversation_summaries.db` through the distro's `\\\\wsl.localhost` home. The row's `workspace_uris` name Linux folders (a distro's agy is a Linux program), so Cwd reads `/home/…`, not a mangled Windows path.\n- The listing carries the summaries row with the file (`wslEntry.Agy`), so a distro conversation is named by its title, and a title agy writes later re-reads it; agy's summaries are held per database, the distros' beside this computer's own.\n- Its calls come from the same transcripts (`agyCallFiles` adds `wslFiles(\"agy\")`), so a distro agy's calls count in usage.\n- Resume is what `resumeCommand` already planned for a distro: `wsl.exe -d '…' --cd '<folder>' … 'agy --conversation <id>'`, with `AgyStart` left out — the Windows twin's key and address are not the distro's.\n\n`TestWSLSessionsListed` covers listing, naming, resume and the calls of a distro agy against the same fixture the local agy tests use; the stopped-distro tests' counts take the three conversations in. Full `internal/sessions` (`-tags nogui`): 649 passed; `docs/subsystems/gateway-sessions.md` updated.\n\nNot done, as the issue says plainly: this was never tried against a real WSL agy — the tests read a fixture tree through the same listing path, and `provider.OpenReadOnly` over the UNC path is the same read the Windows tests of other agents' distro databases exercise. If a real distro's agy lists oddly, that report would tell.\n",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
