     "body": "### Environment\n\nWindows magpie + agents in WSL (repro: omp 18.12.6 on Debian). Self-hosted Langfuse (events-only), OTel on, `sessions: true`. Checked on `origin/main` @ `d6df72a`.\n\n### Symptom\n\nEach call shows up as a lone `gateway` + `chat` pair with no shared session / waterfall / `interaction` span. Host-side agents of the same kinds group fine. ClickHouse: `session_id` empty on all rows; no `langfuse.session.id`.\n\nFor the omp repro, usage already has the right `session` / `native_session` from `x-session-affinity`—so this isn’t “the agent forgot to send a session.”\n\n### Cause\n\n1. `traceLineFiles()` (`internal/sessions/traces.go`) only scans host paths. It never calls `wslFiles`. Sessions/Usage already do for **claude / codex / pi / omp** (the TraceAgent ∩ wslAgents set). The OTel follower doesn’t.\n2. `langfuse.session.id` is only written on follower spans (`otel_wire.go`). Gateway spans never get it, even when `usage.Record.Session` is set.\n\nSame shape as #581’s leftover: mirrored mode no longer drops the gateway trace, but without WSL files in the follower you still get ungrouped gateway/`chat` pairs.\n\n### Suggested fix\n\n- **A:** `traceLineFiles()` append `wslFiles(\"claude\", \"codex\", \"pi\", \"omp\")` (+ test that those WSL paths are included).\n- **B:** when `r.Session != \"\"`, set `langfuse.session.id` on the gateway root span (separate PR; changes wire output for everyone).\n\nNot #1138/#1150 (UI listing), #2284 (Codex Langfuse dupes), or #3595 (agy). Filing an issue first (#3678: PRs collaborators-only).",
